# Airbnb Clone — Project Guidance & AI Rules

This configuration provides lightweight, project-specific rules for AI agents and developer tools working on this codebase.

---

## 1. Core Principles & Independent Implementation
- **No Source Code Copying**: All code must be independently written from scratch using React, Vite, and Vanilla/Tailwind CSS. Reference designs/specs are visual and behavioral targets only.
- **Audit Before Modifying**: Before editing any existing file, always view the complete file content to understand established patterns, props, and schema imports.
- **Ask for Confirmation**: Always ask the user for confirmation before performing breaking architectural changes or deleting existing code files.

---

## 2. React Conventions
- **Functional Components**: Use arrow function components (`const ComponentName = () => { ... }`).
- **Hooks Rules**: Follow React 19 hook guidelines. Never call `setState` synchronously inside a `useEffect` body if the state can be derived during rendering.
- **Prop Interfaces**: Keep component interfaces clean and explicit. Provide sensible default prop values.
- **Context Usage**: Consume shared state via centralized custom hooks (e.g. `useGallery()`). Do not instantiate redundant local state when global context exists.

---

## 3. JavaScript Conventions
- **ES Module Syntax**: Use clean ES6+ imports and exports (`import ... from ...`, `export const ...`, `export default ...`).
- **Centralized Data**: `src/data/property.js` is the SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH. Never hardcode property pricing, images, or host details directly inside components.
- **Utility Functions**: Keep business logic (total pricing math, subsets, categorization) inside pure helper functions exported from `property.js` or `src/utils/`.

---

## 4. Component Organization
```
src/
├── components/
│   ├── gallery/       # Full-viewport Photo Tour gallery view
│   ├── layout/        # Header, Footer, and page shell layouts
│   ├── lightbox/      # Single-photo Lightbox viewer overlay
│   ├── listing/       # Listing page sections (PhotoGrid, BookingCard, HostSection, etc.)
│   └── shared/        # Atomic primitives (Button, IconButton, Avatar, StarRating, Modal)
├── contexts/          # React Context providers and custom hooks
├── hooks/             # Shared custom hooks (useTrapFocus, useLockBodyScroll, etc.)
├── data/              # Centralized property dataset
└── utils/             # Constants and helper utilities
```

---

## 5. Accessibility (a11y) Rules
- **Semantic Buttons**: Interactive elements must use native `<button type="button">`, `<a href="...">`, or React Router `<Link>`.
- **Keyboard Navigation**: All interactive controls must respond to `Enter`, `Space`, `Tab`, `ArrowLeft`, `ArrowRight`, and `Escape`.
- **Focus Indicators**: Enforce crisp focus ring styling (`focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-black` or `focus-visible:ring-white`).
- **Modal Controls**: Modal overlays must implement `role="dialog"`, `aria-modal="true"`, focus trapping (`useTrapFocus`), and background scroll locking (`useLockBodyScroll`).
- **Screen Readers**: Provide descriptive `alt` text on non-decorative images and `aria-hidden="true"` on decorative icons.
- **Heading Hierarchy**: Maintain logical document heading outline (`h1` -> `h2` -> `h3`) without skipping levels.

---

## 6. Visual Fidelity Rules
- **Desktop Specification**: Desktop layout is the primary target. Maintain an `1120px` max content width container.
- **Photo Bento Grid**: 1 Hero image (50% width) + 4 side images in 2x2 grid (50% width) with `12px` outer radius and `8px` gaps.
- **Typography & Colors**:
  - Primary text: `#222222`
  - Secondary text: `#717171`
  - Accent color: `#FF385C` (Airbnb Rausch)
  - Borders: `#EBEBEB` (light), `#DDDDDD` (default), `#B0B0B0` (dark)
- **Subtle Micro-Interactions**: Use hardware-accelerated CSS transitions/keyframes (`heartPop`, `slideUp`, `scaleIn`). Avoid over-animating.

---

## 7. Testing & Build Requirements
- **Verification**: Every code change must be verified by running:
  - `npm run lint` (ESLint rule check)
  - `npm run build` (Vite production bundle compilation)
- **Zero Errors**: Never declare a task complete if linting or build errors remain.

---

## 8. Performance Requirements
- **Code-Splitting**: Heavy overlay views (`PhotoTour`, `Lightbox`) must be code-split using `React.lazy` and `Suspense`.
- **Image Optimization**: High-priority LCP hero images use `loading="eager"`; secondary images use `loading="lazy"`.
- **Zero External UI Dependencies**: Rely on native Tailwind CSS utilities and React state instead of heavy third-party UI libraries.
